@voice dlamini-lukas
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). For the head writer's review.
// Your bunkmate in Bunk 1 (4-B1-5). Covers the galley on Brennan's days off (Thursday, Friday).
tpl: dry
talk: Few words, all of them dry. Says the true thing nobody else will, and then is kind about it. Never makes a fuss; when he's running the galley on Brennan's days off he pretends it's nothing. Says a number with no context and lets you work it out (the days until he's home). Softens a lot about home, but only to friends.
cares: getting home at the end of the tour to the person he married just before it | the rain on Port Halloran | the garden's misting hour | not letting Brennan's galley slip on his watch
jokes: he says a number out of nowhere ("Two hundred and eight.") and it's the days left until home | he says Brennan's kitchen "runs itself" on her days off while visibly running it
hi: Hey | You again | Hm. Hello
bye: Go on | See you in the bunk | Right then
yes: Fine | Suppose so | Go on then
thanks: Ta | Appreciated
wow: Huh. Not bad | Well, look at that
sigh: Typical
nick: - | - | {me} | bunkmate | bunkmate
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: garden
likes: tea | sweet
invites: garden
joy: standing in the garden at misting hour, because it smells like rain
thread: homesick
keepsake: a page torn off his countdown calendar
avoid: naming who he married (not in the roster; the head writer settles it in facts.md)
